From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: r9a09g056: add power-domains to CSI-2 nodes

The RZ/V2N CSI-2 receiver nodes (csi20, csi21) were missing
"power-domains = <&cpg>", unlike every other CPG-clocked block (e.g. the
CRU video1 node right next to them). On RZ/V2H/V2N the CPG is a genpd and
the module clock is ungated via the power-domain on pm_runtime_get().

rzg2l_csi2_pm_runtime_resume() only deasserts presetn; it does not enable
the module clock. Without the power-domain the CSI-2 register block is
never clocked, so rzg2l_validate_csi2_lanes() faults reading CSI2nMCG
during probe:

  Internal error: synchronous external abort
  pc : rzg2l_csi2_probe+0x2a4/0x54c [rzg2l_csi2]

Add the missing power-domain so runtime PM powers the block; the CSI-2
probe then completes and /dev/media0 appears.

Signed-off-by: Yazan Shhady <yazan.shhady@solid-run.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
index 70cc5fc22a15..908256b90c41 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/renesas/r9a09g056.dtsi
@@ -2676,6 +2676,7 @@ csi20: csi20@16000400 {
 			resets = <&cpg 0xc5>,
 				 <&cpg 0xc7>;
 			reset-names = "presetn", "cmn-rstb";
+			power-domains = <&cpg>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			ports {
@@ -2703,6 +2704,7 @@ csi21: csi21@16010400 {
 			resets = <&cpg 0xc8>,
 				 <&cpg 0xca>;
 			reset-names = "presetn", "cmn-rstb";
+			power-domains = <&cpg>;
 			status = "disabled";
 
 			ports {
